{"created": "2026-11-11T21:12:19.137319+00:00", "modified": "2026-11-11T21:12:19.379057+00:00", "id": 24146380, "conceptrecid": "24146379", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.24146380", "conceptdoi": "10.5281/zenodo.24146379", "doi_url": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.24146380", "metadata": {"title": "point-charges", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.24146380", "publication_date": "2026-11-11", "description": "<p>This study reports computer-certified counts of equilibrium points of the electrostatic potential of a handful of point charges, compared with Maxwell's 1873 bound of at most (n-1)^2 points.</p><p>Exact counts, all non-degenerate, are 4 for 3 charges, 9 for 4 charges, 24 for 5 charges, 29 for 6 charges, and 44 for 7 charges, the last proved by the independent verifier only for now.</p><p>Evidence, not proof: no three-charge configuration with more than 4 equilibria, and no four-charge configuration with more than 9, turned up in the searches described in the notes. The work was not reviewed by a person.</p><p>Directed by Ahraz Arifuddin</p><p>Researched and verified by different model families across Gemini, Claude, Grok, OpenAI, and Muse</p><p>Code (*.py) is Apache License 2.0. Text, data and certificates (NOTE.md, README, certificates/, and results/) are Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International (CC BY 4.0); see LICENSE-CC-BY-4.0.</p>", "access_right": "open", "creators": [{"name": "Arifuddin, Ahraz", "affiliation": null}], "keywords": ["electrostatics", "foundation-0", "physics", "point-charges"], "related_identifiers": [{"identifier": "https://github.com/Foundation-0/point-charges", "relation": "isSupplementTo", "resource_type": "software", "scheme": "url"}], "version": "v1.0.0", "custom": {"code:codeRepository": "https://github.com/Foundation-0/point-charges"}, "resource_type": {"title": "Software", "type": "software"}, "license": {"id": "apache2.0"}, "relations": {"version": [{"index": 0, "is_last": true, "parent": {"pid_type": "recid", "pid_value": "24146379"}}]}}, "